# Line endings.
#
# Without this file, Git on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) checks text files out
# with CRLF. That is harmless for TypeScript, but it breaks the shell scripts
# that run inside the emulator's Linux containers: a `#!/bin/sh` shebang becomes
# `#!/bin/sh\r`, and the container fails with a "bad interpreter" error that says
# nothing about line endings.
#
# `text=auto` stores everything with LF in the repository; `eol=lf` also checks
# it out with LF on every platform, so a Windows contributor gets working
# scripts and clean diffs.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the files where CRLF is an actual failure, not cosmetics.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
emulator/ssh/pct text eol=lf

# Never touch binaries.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.tgz binary
*.gz binary
